<title>USA: BMC Industries to buy Brazilian lens maker.</title>
<headline>BMC Industries to buy Brazilian lens maker.</headline>
<dateline>MINNEAPOLIS 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>BMC Industries Inc said Friday its Vision-Ease Lens Inc unit signed a letter of intent to buy Macprado Produtos Oftalmicos Ltda, a Brazilian lens manufacturer and distributor.</p>
<p>Vision-Ease and Corning Inc would be 50-50 partners in the acquisition. The transaction was expected to close in the fourth quarter of this year. Further terms of the deal were not disclosed.</p>
<p>Macprado's had sales of more than $15 million last year, BMC said. Macprado has more than 20 percent of the Brazilian ophthalmic lens market.</p>
<p>-- ((Reuters Chicago Newsdesk 312-408-8787))</p>
